# No native / system dropdowns in product UI

## Why

Native `<select>` / `<datalist>` render platform chrome (macOS blue menus, Windows lists), ignore the
palette, radius, dark mode and motion rules, and cannot be inspected by the background-mode CUA harness.

## Rule

Applies to Studio, the Console (`apps/web`), `@aster-ai-lab/ui`, `@aster-ai-lab/intelligent-ui`, `@aster-ai-lab/form`,
and vanilla shells (e.g. Studio's first-run shell):

1. **Never** ship native `<select>`, `<datalist>` or `document.createElement('select')`.
2. **Use** `SearchSelect` from `@aster-ai-lab/ui` by default:
   - `size="sm"` in toolbars (30px), default size in forms (36px);
   - `searchable={false}` when there are ≤ 8 options;
   - `allowClear={false}` when a value is always required;
   - an explicit `aria-label` (or a visible label), i18n option labels, string values.
3. **Use** `Combobox` only when the trigger must read as a text field.
4. Without React, draw the same anatomy (`SelectControl` in `@aster-ai-lab/form`, the shell picker in
   `apps/studio/src/renderer/shell/studioClient.mjs`).
5. The Radix `Select` composite is legacy: its screens are a shrink-only list in
   `apps/studio/src/renderer/__tests__/noNativeSelect.test.ts`. Do not add a new usage.
6. Visual, keyboard and ARIA contract: `DESIGN.md` §6 "Picker (dropdown)". Rationale and enforcement:
   `docs/development-standards.md` §15, constitution XVI.
7. Tests open the trigger and click the `role="option"` row; never `selectOptions` or a `change` event.
   ACL suites `click` the trigger and `role("option", …)` instead of the `select` action.

Exception: test fixtures whose purpose is to exercise a native control (e.g. `crates/test/fixtures`).

## Quick check

If the open menu looks like the OS / browser default (system blue, checkmark row), it is wrong — replace
it with `SearchSelect`.
